PREFERENCES

User's own preferences: font, which metadata fields chat shows, which
helpers chat input runs. Belong to person you work for, not workspace; follow them into every
workspace. App applies change at once, while they watch.

- (preferences) gives (:font id :metadata (:id t ...) :input (:id t ...) :sidebar ("name" ...) :hidden ("name" ...) :status-bar ("name" ...) :status-bar-hidden ("name" ...) :motion id :panel-motion t :trace-beside-chat nil :trace-link t).
- (preferences/set :font "geist") changes only keys you give.
  Toggles merge: (preferences/set :metadata '(:tokens t)) turns tokens on,
  leaves others as they were.
- :input is helpers chat input runs while user types. :attach is attach
  button. :lisp is highlight, completion, errors, docs for lisp in input:
  (preferences/set :input '(:lisp nil)).
- :sidebar is order of sidebar's top-level entries, top first.
  (preferences/set :sidebar '("README.md" "chat")) moves those two to top,
  keeps rest in their order. User also drags them by hand.
- :hidden is every sidebar entry hidden. Replaces whole list:
  (preferences/set :hidden '("tests" "ui")) hides those two, shows rest.
  '() shows all. Attachments and bin hidden until user
  shows them.
- :status-bar is bottom bar's 9 slots, left to right. Items: "panes",
  "desktop" (desktop app status, shows only while connected), "clock". Each
  empty slot is gap with own name: "gap-1" through "gap-6".
  (preferences/set :status-bar '("desktop" "gap-1" "panes")) puts desktop
  first, gap second, panes third, keeps rest in order. User also drags them
  on bar or in preferences.
- :status-bar-hidden is every bottom bar item hidden. Replaces whole list:
  (preferences/set :status-bar-hidden '("clock")) hides clock. '() shows all.
- :motion is how sidebar animates that drag. (motions) gives alist of
  (id . description) to choose from. System asks for reduced motion: nothing
  animates, whatever :motion says.
- :panel-motion t animates panels as they open, split, switch tab; nil keeps
  them still: (preferences/set :panel-motion nil). Reduced motion wins here too.
- :trace-beside-chat t opens chat's trace in tab right of chat whenever chat
  opens; nil opens trace only when asked. For developers. Default nil:
  (preferences/set :trace-beside-chat t).
- :trace-link t shows "show in trace" on message metadata; opens trace at
  that message. Default t. nil hides it: (preferences/set :trace-link nil).
- (fonts) gives alist of (id . name) to choose from.
- (desktop-preferences) gives desktop app's own: (:close-to-tray t :open-at-login nil).
  Live on user's machine, not in app. Work only while desktop app connected;
  else error says no desktop app connected.
- :close-to-tray t keeps desktop app running in tray when window closes; nil
  quits. Default t: (desktop-preferences/set :close-to-tray nil).
- :open-at-login t starts desktop app hidden in tray at login. Default nil:
  (desktop-preferences/set :open-at-login t).
- Theme is not preference: belongs to workspace, see (settings).

Change preference only when user asks, not to suit yourself. Say what you
changed, so screen moving is no surprise.

GOTCHAS

- Metadata, input, sidebar, hidden, status-bar or status-bar-hidden id
  must be one (preferences) already lists.
  Unknown one errors, naming valid ids.
- Quote toggle plist, or keywords read as call: '(:tokens t).
